// Package dictionary: daily parental-presence allowance (AJPP, wave 3,
// FINISH ajpp-death: D. 544-1..10, R. 544-1..3; D73 transfer: L. 755-33).
// The rules of `02-droit-duree.law` derive the computation-level right from
// the medical channel (certificate + control agreement) and the parental
// leave; `03-plafond-renouvellement.law` carries the 310-day ceiling, the
// exceptional once-renewal and reopening; `04-montants.law` the monthly cap,
// the daily-rate amounts, the expense complement and the special workers;
// `05-non-cumul.law` the nine non-cumulation items with the part-time sick
// exception; `06-devoir-informer.law` the fund information duty.
// `07-durees-decret.law` carries the decree duration mechanics (3-year
// limit, re-exam window and renewal, reopening delay and branches, new
// pathology); `08-montants-decret.law` the pinned decree figures (22-day
// monthly cap, SMIC formula and 2021 BMAF rates, half-day and part-time
// amounts, computed complement threshold, job-seeker flat 22);
// `09-procedure-devoirs.law` the file completeness, the competent service,
// the silence rules and the monthly and expense duties;
// `10-attribution-dom.law` the L. 751-1 collectivity attribution (L. 755-33,
// D73 owner transfer).
//
// KEY DISCIPLINE (engine-bound): every keyed premise arrives with its key
// bound (per-child and per-month keys); free-key generation runs only in
// the latest edition, so no rule generates over a keyed relation with a
// free key (fr.pf.aeeh evidence: pre-2021 silence). The carer link
// conge_presence_parentale carries no key (multi-carer sharing).
//
// DEONTIC MAP OVER PINNED TEXTS ONLY (bytes of 01-sources.law; outside
// them — boundary, not conjecture).
//
//   D1. Duty of the fund to inform. «L'organisme débiteur des prestations
//   familiales est tenu d'informer le demandeur ou le bénéficiaire»
//   (L. 544-10) of the AEEH/PCH award criteria and claim steps. Trigger:
//   leave + open right + debtor link. Performance: the recorded information
//   fact. Window [@2021-01-01, ∞).
//   D2. Duty of the L. 5421-1 job-seeker to declare to France Travail
//   (D. 544-8, para. 3: «portent à la connaissance de l'opérateur France
//   Travail le nombre de jours pris»). Bearer: the job-seeker;
//   beneficiary: the operator body. Window [@2021-01-01, ∞).
//   D3-D7. Monthly supporting-document duties of the five beneficiary
//   classes (D. 544-9 1°-5°: employer attestation for leave-takers and
//   public agents, trainer attestation plus sworn statement for paid
//   trainees, sworn cessation statement for job-seekers, sworn activity
//   interruption statement for non-salaried/VRP). Bearer: the beneficiary;
//   beneficiary: the debtor body. Window [@2021-01-01, ∞). Trigger:
//   beneficiary class + debtor link + concerned month (mois_concerne_ajpp).
//   «Chaque mois au plus» is read as the monthly proof rhythm (frequency
//   ceiling, satisfied by monthly sending; no over-frequency prohibition
//   is modelled). Each duty instance and performance is keyed by the
//   concerned month: a transmission for March never satisfies April.
//   D8. Monthly sworn expense declaration for the L. 544-7 complement
//   (D. 544-10, sentence 1: «pour chaque mois considéré»). Bearer: the
//   allocataire; beneficiary: the debtor body. Window [@2021-01-01, ∞).
//   Month-keyed like D3-D7.
//   D9. Production of the supporting elements on the fund's demand
//   (D. 544-10, sentence 2: «doit être en mesure de produire, à la demande
//   de l'organisme»). Conditional duty, triggered by the recorded demand
//   plus the standing declaration for the concerned month. Window
//   [@2021-01-01, ∞). Month-keyed like D3-D7.
//   D10. Notification of the favourable control opinion on renewal
//   requests (R. 544-3, II, 3°, prev window only: «notifie, dès qu'il en a
//   connaissance, l'avis favorable»). Bearer: the debtor body; beneficiary:
//   the claimant. Window [@2022-04-30, @2024-02-05).
//   Permissions without a named holder stay status heads, not liberties:
//   the re-exam request window (D. 544-2 «peut être demandé», passive),
//   the reopening (D. 544-3 «peut être ouvert à nouveau», passive) and the
//   half-day payment (D. 544-6 «peut être versée», passive).
//   No sanctions in scope. The ARE suspension/reprise (L. 544-8, para. 3)
//   is automatic versement mechanics — package fr.prestations.versement
//   (wave 5), not a power here. R. 544-2 is a competence attribution (the
//   child's health-cost scheme service gives the L. 544-2 agreement), not
//   a new position.
//   L. 544-1 (base right per leave day, L. 1225-62 travail) is SANS_OWNER
//   with a future abrogation (ABROGE_DIFF, end 2027-12-12): boundary quote
//   in REPORT, never cited. The head is grounded on L. 544-2 (certificate +
//   agreement open the right) with the leave as the external channel fact.
//   The D. 544-8 exception («dans les conditions définies à l'article
//   L. 544-1») therefore ends at that boundary: an exception marker, not
//   a payment rule (B-PFAJPP-L544-1-EXCEPTION).
//
// LAYER BOUNDARIES (omission records, not norms):
// B-PFAJPP-TETE: the computation heads are carried by this package on its
// own established facts. fr.pf.core holds parallel principle-level filters
// (beneficie_ajpp, AjppPlafond310, NonCumulAjpp, demandeur_ajpp_informe)
// that are package-internal (§24, not exported): this package cannot read
// them, so it does not; case worlds assert the local symbols and the
// upstream filters stay silent there. Same source facts, no redefinition.
// B-PFAJPP-D544: PARTLY CLOSED by the FINISH ajpp-death wave. Now pinned
// decree text with params and rules: 22 monthly days (D. 544-4),
// 3-year duration per child and pathology (D. 544-1), daily-rate formula
// and 2021 BMAF rates with half-day and part-time amounts (D. 544-6),
// 27.19 % complement threshold and amount (D. 544-7), job-seeker flat 22
// (D. 544-8). Still case inputs with provenance: the retained BMAF euro
// figure (series owned by fr.css.revalorisation; the decree names no
// reference month — B-PFAJPP-BMAF-FIGURE), the net hourly SMIC shn
// (established pre-rounded figure — B-PFAJPP-SHN-NET), the CRDS rate a
// (ordonnance 96-50 art. 14; cross-check against
// fr.prestations.versement TauxCRDSPF is deferred, no import — the
// versement package consumes our brut heads, so importing it would cycle —
// B-PFAJPP-CRDS-TAUX), the R. 522-2 annual ceiling and the R. 532-1
// assessed resources (neighbour articles, out of scope).
// B-PFAJPP-DUREE: PARTLY CLOSED. Modelled now: 3-year limit, re-exam
// request window and renewal within the remaining caps, reopening delay
// and payment branches, new pathology, file completeness, competent
// service, silence-deemed agreement and decision. The reopening routes
// stay separate: D. 544-3 para. 1 reopens within three years while the
// day maximum is unused; L. 544-3 para. 3 (2019: para. 2) reopens only
// beyond the expired maximum duration («Au-delà de la durée maximale»),
// and only that route pays beyond the maximum (D. 544-3 2°). Still open: renewal
// silence before 2022-04-30 (the text then covers only the initial
// request — NEITHER by construction,
// B-PFAJPP-SILENCE-RENOUVELLEMENT-AVANT-2022); death extension mechanics
// (none in the pinned R. 544-x — no rule).
// B-PFAJPP-FORMULE-DIVISION: the D. 544-6 quotient (7*shn)/(1-a) is built
// by one formula rule with the text rounding («arrondi au centième
// d'euro»). Per D75 the pin names no tie-breaking mode: non-tie
// outputs are source-derived (every nearest-mode agrees), exact
// half-cent ties are case-flagged (tie_formule_taux) and stay pending
// (taux_tie_en_attente, B-PFAJPP-TIE-ARRONDI) until the owner records
// a tie policy; the HALF_UP mode argument of ajpp_taux_formule is
// mechanical, never a tie assertion, and no other package's precedent
// is cited as policy. D-42 (08.10.2026): the run qualified the
// division — `/` refuses the non-terminating quotient (INEXACT_DIVISION,
// §58), so the formula is written div_round §50 (exact quotient rounded
// once to the cent); built rates run on Python and Rust.
// B-PFAJPP-TIE-ARRONDI: exact half-cent ties of the D. 544-6 formula
// (D75 source boundary): the rounded rate is not derived; the pending
// head taux_tie_en_attente stands instead. Tie worlds assert
// tie_formule_taux with the external computation as provenance;
// unflagged ties are a case-authoring error, not a legal assertion.
// B-PFAJPP-L544-1-EXCEPTION: D. 544-8 occasional-activity job-seekers are
// paid «dans les conditions définies à l'article L. 544-1» — L. 544-1 is
// SANS_OWNER (boundary quote): exception marker only, no payment rule.
// B-PFAJPP-D544-UN-AN: D. 544-2 still measures the one-year mark as a
// fixed 12 months while L. 544-2 raised the re-exam ceiling to 14 months
// in 2026: decoded as written (12 in the D. 544-2 branch), proposed D-NN.
// B-PFAJPP-ARE: ARE suspension/reprise mechanics (L. 544-8, para. 3;
// L. 5421-1 travail, external) — versement package (wave 5).
// B-PFAJPP-PARTAGE: designation/sharing between the two members (L. 544-4
// «à l'un ou aux deux membres du couple», L. 544-6 modulation) — mechanism
// owned by fr.pf.af; carer links arrive per case.
// B-PFAJPP-ARRONDI: no cent-rounding rule in scope; Money keeps exact
// Decimal products, no silent rounding (fr.pf.aeeh evidence).
// B-PFAJPP-OF: OpenFisca AJPP parameters (frozen 2006-06-05) are parameters
// without a model upstream: documentary measurement only (REPORT +
// tests/foreign/openfisca/NOTE.md), never regressions.
// B-PFAJPP-DOM-L751: L. 755-33 extends the AJPP attribution to the
// collectivités listed in L. 751-1; the L. 751-1 list itself (which
// territories) is out of scope — residence arrives as a case fact
// with provenance. Pre-2021 DOM attribution is a prev-coverage gap.
// B-PFAJPP-ENVELOPPE-QUALIFIEE (F05-01): monthly daily amounts
// require the qualified envelope plus the month conformity. Initial
// / once-renewal branch: ajpp_dans_limite (first 310 OR renewal
// 310 — no blanket lifetime cap) and ajpp_duree_dans_limite (3
// years per child and pathology). Beyond-maximum reopening branch:
// droit_rouvert + versement_au_dela_max (fresh D. 544-1
// application; old exhaustion/expiry do not block). Monthly:
// mensuel_dans_limite for daily paths (L. 544-4 / D. 544-4 22),
// forfait_22_conforme for flat paths (D. 544-8 22). Demi-day and
// part-time amounts require the envelope only (monthly conversion
// boundary B-PFAJPP-DEMI-PLAFOND).
// B-PFAJPP-DEMI-PLAFOND: D. 544-4 caps «le nombre d'allocations
// journalières versées ... au titre d'un mois civil» at 22. The
// pinned bytes do not convert half-day allowances (D. 544-6 demi)
// or part-time days not worked into that count — no monthly gate
// for demi/part-time amounts, envelope only. No invented 44-half
// or 22-not-worked cap.
// B-PFAJPP-ROUVERTURE-COMPTEUR: the beyond-maximum reopened right
// is paid «dans la limite d'une nouvelle application de la durée
// maximale» (D. 544-3 2°). No fresh day counter for the reopened
// envelope is modelled (jours_ajpp_verses counts the original
// envelope); reopening amounts require monthly + droit_rouvert +
// versement_au_dela_max, no new 310 check. A fresh counter needs
// an owner D-NN and a new empirical input.
// B-PFAJPP-NOUVELLE-PATHOLOGIE-COMPTEUR: D. 544-1 limits per child
// AND pathology, but jours_ajpp_verses is per child. A new
// pathology gets no separate fresh counter here; new-pathology
// amounts would gate on the old child counter. No amount tests
// for new pathology; a per-cause counter is future work.
//
// INPUT CONTRACT (engine has no absence test): exactly one taux input
// (normal / majoré / modulé) per child-month; exactly one of
// {jours_ajpp_mois, jours_forfaitaires} per child-month; for non-cumul
// exactly one of {one motif fact, the part-time pair, neither} per
// beneficiary (run the motif tests one motif per world). Decree layer:
// exactly one of {couple rate, single rate} per child for the 2021 BMAF
// rates; exactly one treatment start and one foreseeable duration per
// child; exactly one opening month and one relapse month per reopening
// case; exactly one cause duration per child in reopening/expiry
// worlds (the expiry head projects the cause); exactly one of
// {demande_initiale, demande_renouvellement} per
// silence case; month facts are Integer months on one case-local scale.
// Flat-day worlds assert the pinned D. 544-8 figure (22 per month for
// the L. 544-8 para. 2 class, both pinned versions) outside the
// L. 544-1 exception; any other asserted count leaves the decree
// conformance head silent.
// Monthly-duty worlds assert the concerned month per beneficiary
// (mois_concerne_ajpp, first-of-month Date; one child each — cross-child
// months need separate worlds). Formula worlds with an exact half-cent
// tie assert tie_formule_taux, established by external computation
// (B-PFAJPP-TIE-ARRONDI). Amount worlds assert the envelope history
// for enveloppe_ajpp_qualifiee (F05-01): cumulative jours_ajpp_verses
// (or second-envelope jours_ajpp_second_enveloppe with a granted
// renewal) plus duree_versement_ajpp per child and cause; reopening
// amount worlds assert the expiry-gated droit_rouvert route instead
// (old exhaustion/expiry do not block). Monthly conformity needs no
// extra fact where the decree 22 path applies (daily days <= 22,
// flat days == 22); the retained-max path needs plafond_mensuel_retenu.
// Worlds without envelope history leave amounts NEITHER by
// construction (no negative from unknown).
//
// Scenarios: tests/ajpp-*.lawtest (families fr.pf.ajpp#droit-duree,
// #plafond-renouvellement, #montants, #non-cumul, #devoir-informer,
// #durees-decret, #montants-decret, #procedure-devoirs, #attribution-dom
// in law.toml):
// inputs→value; boundary pairs (310 edges, renewal window, 2018/2025
// lists, part-time exception, 2023-H1 majoration, 3-year duration,
// re-exam window, reopening delay and max, beyond-maximum expiry gate,
// 22-day cap, formula rate,
// tie pending, complement threshold equality, silence months, renewal
// silence generations, monthly-duty months, DOM residence,
// F05-01 amount qualification (monthly overflow, flat 15, 311 spent,
// duration spent, unknown history, renewal and reopening positives)).
// ajpp-blind-22 pins the D-38 class (c) contract: the 2018
// cumulation refusal carries no parental-leave premise (exact L. 544-9
// quote in the test header).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.ajpp version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-ajpp";

import fr.pf.core version "0.1.0";

pub enum MotifNonCumul2018 {
    label fr official "cause de non-cumul 2018-2025 (L. 544-9, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "non-cumulation ground 2018-2025 (L. 544-9, established fact)";
    MATERNITE_PATERNITE_ADOPTION,
    INTERRUPTION_ACTIVITE,
    MALADIE_AT,
    CHOMAGE,
    VIEILLESSE_INVALIDITE,
    PREPARE,
    AEEH_COMPLEMENT_MAJO,
    AAH,
    PCH_ELEMENT
}

pub enum MotifNonCumul2025 {
    label fr official "cause de non-cumul depuis 2026 (L. 544-9 2025, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "non-cumulation ground from 2026 (L. 544-9 2025, established fact)";
    MATERNITE_PATERNITE_NAISSANCE,
    INTERRUPTION_ACTIVITE_623_2,
    MALADIE_AT,
    CHOMAGE,
    VIEILLESSE_INVALIDITE,
    PREPARE,
    AEEH_COMPLEMENT_MAJO,
    AAH,
    PCH_ELEMENT
}

pub relation certificat_gravite(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "certificat médical détaillé : particulière gravité et caractère indispensable d'une présence soutenue et de soins contraignants, durée prévisible du traitement (L. 544-2, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "detailed medical certificate: particular gravity and indispensable sustained presence and constraining care, foreseeable treatment duration (L. 544-2, established fact)";
}

pub relation avis_favorable_controle(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "avis favorable du service du contrôle médical L. 315-1 ou du régime spécial (L. 544-2, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "favourable agreement of the L. 315-1 medical control service or special scheme (L. 544-2, established fact)";
}

pub relation avis_en_attente(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "avis du contrôle médical demandé, en attente (avance L. 544-3, fait du dossier)";
    label en unofficial "medical control agreement requested, pending (L. 544-3 advance, case fact)";
}

pub relation conge_presence_parentale(p: fr.pf.core::Personne, e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "congé de présence parentale L. 1225-62 travail (ou règles agents publics) pris pour l'enfant (hors champ, fait du dossier)";
    label en unofficial "L. 1225-62 labour-code parental presence leave (or public-agent rules) taken for the child (out of scope, case fact)";
}

pub relation echeance_reexamen(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant, mois: Integer) kind empirical {
    key(e);
    label fr official "échéance de réexamen fixée par le médecin, en mois (L. 544-2, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "re-examination deadline set by the doctor, in months (L. 544-2, established fact)";
}

pub relation jours_ajpp_verses(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant, jours: Integer) kind empirical {
    key(e);
    label fr official "allocations journalières versées, première enveloppe, constatées par l'organisme (L. 544-3, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "daily allowances paid, first envelope, recorded by the body (L. 544-3, established fact)";
}

pub relation jours_ajpp_second_enveloppe(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant, jours: Integer) kind empirical {
    key(e);
    label fr official "allocations journalières versées au titre du renouvellement unique, constatées par l'organisme (L. 544-3, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "daily allowances paid under the once-renewal, recorded by the body (L. 544-3, established fact)";
}

pub relation nouveau_certificat(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "nouveau certificat médical attestant le caractère indispensable de la poursuite (L. 544-3 al. 2, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "new medical certificate attesting the indispensable continuation (L. 544-3 para. 2, established fact)";
}

pub relation accord_controle_renouvellement(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "accord du contrôle médical au renouvellement unique (L. 544-3 al. 2, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "medical control agreement to the once-renewal (L. 544-3 para. 2, established fact)";
}

pub relation avant_terme_initial(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "renouvellement demandé avant la fin du terme initialement fixé (L. 544-3 al. 2, fait du dossier)";
    label en unofficial "renewal requested before the end of the initially set term (L. 544-3 para. 2, case fact)";
}

pub relation rechute_pathologie(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "rechute ou récidive de la pathologie au titre de laquelle le droit avait été ouvert (L. 544-3 al. 3, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "relapse or recurrence of the pathology for which the right was opened (L. 544-3 para. 3, established fact)";
}

pub relation gravite_persistante(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant) kind empirical {
    label fr official "gravité de la pathologie nécessitant toujours présence soutenue et soins contraignants (L. 544-3 al. 3, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "pathology gravity still requiring sustained presence and constraining care (L. 544-3 para. 3, established fact)";
}

pub relation jours_ajpp_mois(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant, mois: Date, jours: Integer) kind empirical {
    key(e, mois);
    label fr official "allocations journalières du mois civil, constatées par l'organisme (L. 544-4, fait établi)";
    label en unofficial "daily allowances of the calendar month, recorded by the body (L. 544-4, established fact)";
}

pub relation jours_forfaitaires(e: fr.pf.core::Enfant, mois: Date, jours: Integer) kind empirical {
    key(e, mois);
    label fr official "jours forfaitaires du mois du demandeur d'emploi ou en formation (L. 544-8 al. 2, D. 544-8 épinglé : 22, hors exception L. 544-1, fait du dossier)";
    label en unofficial "flat days of the month of the job-seeker or trainee (L. 544-8 para. 2, pinned D. 544-8: 22, outside the L. 544-1 exception, case fact)";
}

